{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/68", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What does On-going basis for a term of 12 months mean?\", \"response\": \"On-going basis for a term of 12 months means that the contract is valid for a period of 12 months and can be renewed after that. It is a common practice for companies to sign contracts with their clients for a specific period of time, such as 12 months, and then renew them on an annual basis. This allows both the company and the client to evaluate the performance of the contract and make changes if necessary.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/523", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what's the best extension from chrome to share chats from Chat GPT?\", \"response\": \"I'm sorry for any confusion, but as of my current knowledge, there is no specific Chrome extension designed to share chats from a hypothetical Chat GPT application. However, you can still share chats or conversations from a web application using the built-in sharing functionality of Chrome or by using general-purpose screen capture or selection tools.\\n\\nHere's how you can do it using Chrome's built-in sharing feature:\\n\\n1. Click on the three-dot menu in the top-right corner of your Chrome browser.\\n2. Hover over \\\"Share...\\\".\\n3. Choose the method you want to use to share, such as \\\"Email\\\", \\\"Message\\\", or any other installed applications that support sharing.\\n\\nIf you want to share a specific part of the chat, you might need to use a screen capture or selection tool. There are many options available, both free and paid, such as:\\n\\n* Awesome Screenshot: This is a popular Chrome extension for screen capture and annotation.\\n* Lightshot: Another useful tool for quick screenshots and sharing.\\n* Full Page Screen Capture: As the name suggests, this extension captures full-page screenshots.\\n\\nRemember to only share content that respects the privacy and rights of all involved parties.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/112", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Can you recommend a good calendar / schedule API service that i can implement on my website. The requirements are:\\n1. I can create post API calls that can create events with attendees. \\n2. I can create get api calls that returns events for a specific user\\n3. I can set timeslots for when a user is available to be booked\\n4. I can book into available timeslots on a user\", \"response\": \"There are several calendar and schedule API services available that can meet your requirements. Here are a few options to consider:\\n\\n1. Google Calendar API: The Google Calendar API allows you to create, read, and update events in a user's Google Calendar. You can also set time slots for availability and book appointments. The API is easy to use and has a wide range of features, making it a great choice for your project.\\n\\n2. Microsoft Graph API: The Microsoft Graph API provides access to a wide range of Microsoft services, including Outlook, Office 365, and Azure Active Directory. You can use the API to create, read, and update events in a user's calendar, as well as set availability and book appointments.\\n\\n3. Calendly API: Calendly is a scheduling platform that allows users to create and manage events and appointments. The Calendly API allows you to integrate the platform with your website, so that users can book appointments directly from your site. You can also use the API to set availability and book appointments for specific time slots.\\n\\n4. ScheduleOnce API: ScheduleOnce is a scheduling platform that allows users to create and manage events and appointments. The ScheduleOnce API allows you to integrate the platform with your website, so that users can book appointments directly from your site. You can also use the API to set availability and book appointments for specific time slots.\\n\\nThese are just a few of the many calendar and schedule API services available. Each service has its own set of features and pricing, so be sure to evaluate your options and choose the one that best meets your needs.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/504", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What's the answer to the life, the universe, and everything?\", \"response\": \"The answer to the life, the universe, and everything, as famously mentioned in the \\\"Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\\\" by Douglas Adams, is 42. While this answer may seem absurd or nonsensical, it has become a popular cultural reference and is often used as a joke or a tongue-in-cheek answer to deep questions. In the story, the answer 42 is calculated by a supercomputer named Deep Thought, which is asked to find the meaning of life, and after much contemplation, it suggests the answer is 42, leading to much confusion and frustration for the characters in the story. While the answer may not be satisfying or make practical sense, it has become a part of popular culture and is often used as a fun way to acknowledge the absurdity of trying to find a definitive answer to complex or philosophical questions.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/209", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Write us a complex movie plot disney styled with a bit WWII nazi document style, called suricates 2 about the suricates from lion king\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe kingdom of hyenas is threatened by the mighty warlord Suricate, and his cruel army of jackals. The brave suricates must band together to overcome this evil threat, and restore peace and prosperity to the land. The leader of the suricates, the wise and courageous Rina, gathers her brave warriors for a daring battle against Suricate and his jackal army. In a dramatic battle scene, the suricates prevail over the jackals, and Suricate is banished from the kingdom. The land is at peace once again, and the suricates live happily ever after.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nnow write it in rhymes\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe suricates must band together and strike back with might,\\n To defeat Suricate and his army of jackals, so dire and bright.\\n The evil warlord threatens the kingdom of hyenas, and we must do what we can,\\n To restore peace and prosperity to the land, with valor and skill and with good plan.\\n The suricates are wise and brave, and with Rina as our wise leader,\\n We will overcome this threat and Suricate, and make our land once more a paradise to see and cherish.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nnow make it a funky 90s hip hop song\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWe're the suricates, from the land of hyenas,\\n We fight for peace and justice, in a war of good versus evil.\\n We'll do what it takes to defeat our enemy,\\n Suricate and his jackals, so cruel and sly.\\n The suricates are tough and wise, with valor and with skill,\\n We will restore peace and prosperity to the land, so it's beautiful and lively.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nmake these suricates fight crabs from space with triceratops in rockets\", \"response\": \"The suricates are ready to fight,\\n Against the crabs from space, so bright.\\n With triceratops in their rockets,\\n They're ready to take on this new threat, so hot.\\n The crabs from space are a force to be reckoned with,\\n But the suricates are tough and won't give in.\\n They'll use their skills and their wits,\\n To defeat the crabs and save the land, so fit.\\n With their rockets and triceratops by their side,\\n The suricates are ready for this new ride.\\n They'll fight with all their might,\\n And restore peace to the land, so right.\\n So let's join the suricates in their fight,\\n Against the crabs from space, so bright.\\n With triceratops in their rockets,\\n They're ready to take on this new threat, so hot.\\n The suricates are tough and wise, with valor and with skill,\\n They'll restore peace to the land, and make it beautiful and lively.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/912", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"for f(x)=(3x-9)/(x^2-7x+12), determine the vertical asymptote, horizontal asymptote, x intercept, and y intercept and explain your reasoning\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe vertical asymptote occurs when the denominator of f(x) equals 0, which happens when x=3. The horizontal asymptote occurs when the numerator of f(x) equals 0, which happens when x=4. The x-intercept occurs when f(x)=0, which happens when x=1. The y-intercept occurs when f(x)=1, which happens when x=0. These values can all be explained by examining the graph of f(x), which shows a vertical asymptote at x=3, a horizontal asymptote at y=3/4, an x-intercept at x=1, and a y-intercept at y=0.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThe denominator equals 0 when x=4 as well, so why isn't there an asymptote at x=4? Another question: the numerator and denominator have a common factor of (x-3), are we sure this results in a vertical asymptote\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, you are correct that there should be an asymptote at x=4 as well. I apologize for the error, I will correct the previous answer. The common factor of (x-3) in the numerator and denominator of f(x) results in a hole at x=3, rather than an asymptote.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nI was under the impression that there can't be an asymptote AND a hole at the same x value. Am I wrong? If I am correct, which is it, a hole or asymptote when x=3?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYou are correct that there cannot be an asymptote and a hole at the same x-value. In this case, the factor of (x-3) creates a hole at x=3, rather than an asymptote. The vertical asymptote occurs at x=3.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIs the horizontal asymptote y=0 or y=3/4?\", \"response\": \"The horizontal asymptote is y=3/4. I apologize for the error in the previous answer.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/917", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"hi gpt\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHello! How can I help you today?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHow hotel companies charge marketing fee like hotel.com\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI’m glad you asked! I know this one. They charge a marketing fee so they can spend more money on advertising and increase their profits. And then the increased profits go to the shareholders, who are mostly big hotel chains and hotel companies.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncan you give me any reference or source to back up this statement?\", \"response\": \"Yes, here are some references and sources to support the statement that hotel companies charge marketing fees to increase their profits and benefit their shareholders:\\n \\n\\n 1. A study by the American Hotel & Lodging Association found that hotels charge an average of 2-10% of the room rate as a marketing fee, which is used to fund advertising and promotional activities. The study also found that hotels with higher marketing fees tend to have higher occupancy rates and revenue per available room (RevPAR).\\n \\n\\n 2. A report by the consulting firm PwC found that hotel companies are increasingly focusing on maximizing profits and shareholder value, and that marketing fees are one way to achieve this goal. The report notes that hotels use marketing fees to fund advertising campaigns and other initiatives that drive demand and increase revenue.\\n \\n\\n 3. A study by the Cornell University School of Hotel Administration found that hotels with higher marketing fees tend to have higher profits and shareholder returns. The study also found that hotels with higher marketing fees tend to have more loyal customers and better brand recognition.\\n \\n\\n 4. A report by the research firm Skift found that hotel companies are increasingly using marketing fees to fund digital advertising and other online marketing efforts. The report notes that hotels are using data and analytics to target their marketing efforts more effectively and drive higher returns on investment.\\n \\n\\n Overall, these sources suggest that hotel companies charge marketing fees as a way to increase their profits and benefit their shareholders. By funding advertising and promotional activities, hotels can drive demand and increase revenue, which ultimately leads to higher profits and shareholder returns.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/1021", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"myanmar and the Rohingya and international criminal justice\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThere have been many atrocities in Myanmar against the Rohingya, and some have argued that it is a genocide. The UN has set up an investigation into the crimes against the Rohingyas, and there is talk of prosecution.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHas anything been done to prosecute\", \"response\": \"Yes, there have been efforts to prosecute those responsible for the atrocities committed against the Rohingya in Myanmar. In 2018, the United Nations Fact-Finding Mission on Myanmar released a report that found evidence of widespread and systematic human rights violations committed by the Myanmar military against the Rohingya, including murder, rape, and torture. The report called for the prosecution of top military officials for genocide, crimes against humanity, and war crimes.\\n \\n\\n In response to the report, the International Criminal Court (ICC) opened an investigation into the situation in Myanmar in 2019. The ICC has jurisdiction over crimes committed in Myanmar because Bangladesh, where many Rohingya refugees have fled, is a member of the ICC. The investigation is ongoing, and it is not yet clear who will be charged or when the trial will begin.\\n \\n\\n In addition to the ICC investigation, there have been calls for the establishment of an international tribunal to specifically address the crimes committed against the Rohingya. However, this has not yet been established.\\n \\n\\n It is important to note that the Myanmar government has not cooperated with the ICC investigation and has denied the allegations of human rights abuses against the Rohingya. The situation remains complex and ongoing, and it is unclear what the outcome of the ICC investigation and other efforts to prosecute those responsible for the atrocities will be.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/247", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"create test case for the below requirements\\nAs an unregistered/ new user, I want to sign in to IHV app using mobile number so that I can generate OTP and access the features of the app\\nGiven unregistered/new user click on IHV app.\\nAnd user should be able to see the logo of Optimal Oncology on the screen.\\nAnd user should get navigated to the Sign in screen.\\nAnd user should able to see logo of Optimal Oncology and the text below, \\\"Enter your Mobile Number\\\".  with the title Sign in \\nAnd user should be able to see text box with place holder \\\"Mobile Number\\\".\\nAnd user should be able to input only numbers (0-9) in the text box.\\nAnd user should able to see red error message below \\\"Please enter a valid mobile number\\\" if user count not equals to 10. \\nUser cannot enter any inputs other than numbers (alphabets, special characters are not allowed/enabled to be entered).\\n\\nWhen user enter the mobile number and click on \\\"GET OTP\\\" button.\\nThen user should receive 6 digit OTP to the entered mobile number.\\nAnd user should get navigated to OTP verification screen.\\n\\nAnd user should able to see logo of Optimal Oncology and the text below, \\\"Welcome 9123456789\\\" (Welcome username for existing user), \\\"Enter the OTP sent to 9123456789\\\" and a text box to enter OTP. \\nAnd user should be able to enter OTP manually and click on \\\"VERIFY & CONTINUE\\\".\\n\\nScenario 1\\nWhen user enters correct OTP\\nThen the user should get landed in \\\"Personal Info\\\" Screen if the user is a new user. User should land into home screen if the user is an existing user.\\n\\nScenario 2\\nWhen user enters incorrect OTP\\nThen user should able to see red error message below \\\"Enter valid OTP\\\"\\n\\nScenario 3\\nDisplay below message after 30 sec if user didn���t enter OTP, \\\"Didn���t receive OTP? Resend\\\" with a snack bar message \\\"Timed out\\\". \\nWhen \\\"Resend\\\" is clicked, display snack bar \\\"OTP sent successfully\\\"\\n\\nScenario 4\\nWhen user types the values and then deletes, display error message \\\"Mobile number cannot be empty\\\" for mobile field, \\\"OTP cannot be empty\\\" for OTP field\\n\\nScenario 5\\nGET OTP button should be enabled only when the mobile number field is entered with 10 digits. Until the count is 10, GET OTP is disabled, and a message to be displayed \\\"Please enter a valid mobile number\\\".\", \"response\": \"Here's a test case for the given requirements:\\n\\nTest Case for IHV App Sign In Using Mobile Number\\n\\nPurpose: To ensure that the IHV app sign in process using mobile number works as expected for both new and existing users.\\n\\nScenario 1: Successful Sign In for New User\\n\\n    Given an unregistered/new user opens the IHV app\\n    And the user sees the Optimal Oncology logo on the screen\\n    And the user is navigated to the sign in screen\\n    When the user enters a valid mobile number (e.g. 9123456789) into the text box and clicks \\\"GET OTP\\\"\\n    Then the user should receive a 6-digit OTP to the entered mobile number\\n    And the user is navigated to the OTP verification screen\\n    When the user enters the correct OTP into the text box and clicks \\\"VERIFY & CONTINUE\\\"\\n    Then the user should be landed in the \\\"Personal Info\\\" screen\\n    And the user is prompted to enter their personal information\\n\\nScenario 2: Successful Sign In for Existing User\\n\\n    Given an existing user opens the IHV app\\n    And the user sees the Optimal Oncology logo on the screen\\n    And the user is navigated to the sign in screen\\n    When the user enters their mobile number (e.g. 9123456789) into the text box and clicks \\\"GET OTP\\\"\\n    Then the user should receive a 6-digit OTP to the entered mobile number\\n    And the user is navigated to the OTP verification screen\\n    When the user enters the correct OTP into the text box and clicks \\\"VERIFY & CONTINUE\\\"\\n    Then the user should be landed in the home screen\\n    And the user sees a welcome message with their mobile number (e.g. \\\"Welcome 9123456789\\\")\\n\\nScenario 3: Incorrect OTP Entry\\n\\n    Given an existing user opens the IHV app\\n    And the user sees the Optimal Oncology logo on the screen\\n    And the user is navigated to the sign in screen\\n    When the user enters their mobile number (e.g. 9123456789) into the text box and clicks \\\"GET OTP\\\"\\n    Then the user should receive a 6-digit OTP to the entered mobile number\\n    And the user is navigated to the OTP verification screen\\n    When the user enters an incorrect OTP into the text box and clicks \\\"VERIFY & CONTINUE\\\"\\n    Then the user should see an error message \\\"Enter valid OTP\\\"\\n    And the user is prompted to enter the correct OTP\\n\\nScenario 4: OTP Time Out and Resend\\n\\n    Given an existing user opens the IHV app\\n    And the user sees the Optimal Oncology logo on the screen\\n    And the user is navigated to the sign in screen\\n    When the user enters their mobile number (e.g. 9123456789) into the text box and clicks \\\"GET OTP\\\"\\n    Then the user should receive a 6-digit OTP to the entered mobile number\\n    And the user is navigated to the OTP verification screen\\n    When the user does not enter the OTP within 30 seconds\\n    Then the user should see a message \\\"Didn't receive OTP? Resend\\\" with a snack bar message \\\"Timed out\\\"\\n    And the \\\"Resend\\\" button is clicked\\n    Then the user should see a snack bar message \\\"OTP sent successfully\\\"\\n\\nScenario 5: Error Messages for Empty Fields\\n\\n    Given an existing user opens the IHV app\\n    And the user sees the Optimal Oncology logo on the screen\\n    And the user is navigated to the sign in screen\\n    When the user enters an empty mobile number into the text box and clicks \\\"GET OTP\\\"\\n    Then the user should see an error message \\\"Mobile number cannot be empty\\\"\\n    And the \\\"GET OTP\\\" button remains disabled\\n    When the user enters an empty OTP into the text box and clicks \\\"VERIFY & CONTINUE\\\"\\n    Then the user should see an error message \\\"OTP cannot be empty\\\"\\n    And the \\\"VERIFY & CONTINUE\\\" button remains disabled\\n\\nNote: These are just a few of the possible test scenarios for the IHV app sign in using mobile number. The actual test suite may include more scenarios based on the specific requirements and use cases of the app.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/358", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Health ebook\", \"response\": \"Sure! Here are some tips for staying healthy:\\n\\n1. Eat a balanced diet: Eating a variety of fruits, vegetables, whole grains, lean proteins, and healthy fats can help you maintain a healthy weight and reduce your risk of chronic diseases such as heart disease, diabetes, and cancer. Try to limit your intake of processed foods, sugary drinks, and excessive amounts of salt.\\n\\n2. Exercise regularly: Regular physical activity is important for overall health and well-being. Aim for at least 30 minutes of moderate-intensity exercise most days of the week. This can include activities such as walking, jogging, swimming, cycling, or dancing. Strength training and stretching exercises can also help improve your overall fitness and reduce your risk of injury.\\n\\n3. Get enough sleep: Sleep is crucial for maintaining good physical and mental health. Adults should aim for 7-9 hours of sleep per night. Try to establish a regular sleep schedule and create a relaxing bedtime routine to help you wind down and get a good night's sleep.\\n\\n4. Manage stress: Chronic stress can have a negative impact on your physical and mental health. Try to identify the sources of stress in your life and take steps to manage or reduce them. This can include practicing relaxation techniques such as deep breathing, meditation, or yoga, or engaging in activities that you find enjoyable and relaxing.\\n\\n5. Stay hydrated: Drinking enough water is important for maintaining good health. Aim to drink at least 8 glasses of water per day to help keep your body hydrated and functioning properly.\\n\\n6. Maintain good hygiene: Regular hand washing, brushing your teeth, and other hygiene practices can help prevent the spread of germs and infections. Make sure to wash your hands frequently, especially before eating or preparing food, and after using the bathroom.\\n\\n7. Get regular check-ups: Regular check-ups with your healthcare provider can help identify any health issues early on and allow you to take steps to manage or treat them. Make sure to schedule regular check-ups for yourself and your family, and don't hesitate to seek medical attention if you are experiencing any concerning symptoms.\\n\\n8. Stay informed: Staying up-to-date on the latest health information and research can help you make informed decisions about your health and well-being. Read articles, books, or websites on health topics that interest you, or talk to a healthcare provider or nutritionist to learn more about specific health concerns you may have.\\n\\n9. Practice safe habits: Practicing safe habits can help prevent the spread of infections and diseases. This can include wearing seat belts, using condoms during sexual activity, getting vaccinated against preventable diseases, and avoiding risky behaviors such as smoking, excessive alcohol consumption, or drug use.\\n\\n10. Take care of your mental health: Mental health is just as important as physical health. If you are experiencing symptoms of anxiety or depression, talk to a mental health professional or seek support from a trusted friend or family member. Regular exercise, relaxation techniques, and engaging in activities that you find enjoyable can also help improve your mental well-being.\\n\\nRemember, taking care of your health is an ongoing process and it's never too late to start making positive changes. By incorporating these tips into your daily routine, you can help improve your overall health and well-being and reduce your risk of developing chronic diseases and other health issues.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/998", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I am using OpenAI's text completion API. Is there any way can make API remember what user said earlier like a conversation here?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, you can include a context field when making a request to the API. This field should be a string containing previously-generated text from the conversation, which will be used as context for the new request. For example, if you previously requested the text “What is the capital of France?” and the response was “Paris”, then you could use this context in a new request to ask “What is the capital of Germany?”, and the API will respond with “Berlin”.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWill context cost my token?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, including context will consume one token from your token limit. However, using context can be very helpful in reducing the total number of tokens consumed by a long conversation, since it allows you to ask follow-up questions without having to re-ask earlier questions.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWill context limit by 4096 token per request?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, context is limited to 4096 tokens per request. This means that if you want to use context in a large conversation, you will need to split the conversation into multiple requests, each of which uses context from the previous request.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIf I want a model base on lots of text data as it's background knowledge. How can I use API service to do that?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYou can train your own custom model by sending large amounts of training data to the API. This data can be in the form of text, or in the form of prompt/completion pairs. After training your model on this data, you can then use the API to generate new text based on your model.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nDoes training data request prompt/completion format or it could be only text?\", \"response\": \"The training data can be in either format. If you provide text, the API will automatically split it into prompts and completions. However, if you want to provide specific prompts and completions, you can use the prompt/completion format to control the training data more precisely.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/371", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"How to better understand differences between good design and bad design?\", \"response\": \"The difference between good design and bad design can be subjective and dependent on the context and purpose of the design. However, some general principles can help in understanding the differences between good and bad design.\\n\\nGood design typically prioritizes the user's needs and goals, is aesthetically pleasing, and is easy to use and understand. It is also functional, efficient, and takes into account the context in which it will be used. Good design often has a clear purpose and is well-planned, with attention to detail and a consistent design language throughout.\\n\\nBad design, on the other hand, often ignores the user's needs and is difficult to use and understand. It may be visually unappealing, poorly planned, and lacking in attention to detail. Bad design can also be inefficient, confusing, and frustrating for users.\\n\\nSome specific examples of good design include the iPhone's user interface, the design of the Toyota Prius, and the layout of a well-designed website. Examples of bad design include confusing or poorly designed interfaces, uncomfortable furniture, and poorly designed websites that are difficult to navigate.\\n\\nIn summary, good design prioritizes the user's needs, is aesthetically pleasing, and is functional and efficient. Bad design ignores the user's needs, is difficult to use, and is often poorly planned and executed.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/368", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"list down all the different industries that may require customer service, for example, airline industry\", \"response\": \"Here are some of the industries that may require customer service:\\n\\n1. Airlines\\n2. Banking and financial services\\n3. Consumer electronics\\n4. E-commerce\\n5. Healthcare\\n6. Hospitality\\n7. Insurance\\n8. IT services\\n9. Telecom\\n10. Utilities\\n\\nThese are just a few examples, and the list can go on depending on the type of business and the services they provide. Customer service is an essential part of any organization that interacts with customers, whether it's in person, over the phone, or online.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/670", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what is yoga\", \"response\": \"Yoga is a physical, mental, and spiritual practice that originated in ancient India. It involves a combination of physical postures (asanas), breathing techniques (pranayama), meditation, and ethical principles (yamas and niyamas). The goal of yoga is to promote physical and mental well-being, cultivate mindfulness and self-awareness, and achieve a state of spiritual enlightenment.\\n\\nThere are many different styles of yoga, each with its own unique focus and techniques. Some popular styles include Hatha yoga, which focuses on physical postures and breathing exercises; Vinyasa yoga, which involves flowing sequences of postures coordinated with the breath; and Ashtanga yoga, which is a more rigorous style that involves a set series of postures.\\n\\nIn addition to its physical and mental health benefits, yoga is also considered a spiritual practice in many traditions. It is often used as a tool for self-discovery, personal growth, and connection with the divine.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/853", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Rewrite the text in order to make it sound more rude. However do not change the original meaning and intent of the text. Maintain a good format free from grammatical errors. \\n\\nReference Text: The Rector is the academic head of the University and in this role chairs the Senate )the highest academic body of the university). The Rector holds all the authority required to fulfill this role in accordance with the University Constitution and General Statutes, as well as the Academic Statutes.\\n\\nThe Rector is elected by the Senate for a period of 4 years.\\n\\nAll academic bodies within the institution are under the Rector, as follows:\\n\\nFaculties – Faculty of  Humanities and Social Sciences, Faculty of Health Sciences, Faculty of Natural Sciences, Faculty of Engineering Sciences, Guilford Glazer Faculty of Business and Management, The Jacob Blaustein Institutes for Desert Research.\\n\\nUniversity Institutes &  Research Centers – The National Institute for Biotechnology in the Negev, Ben-Gurion Research Institute for the Study of Israel and Zionism, Ilse Katz Institute for Nanoscale Science & Technology, Heksherim Research Institute for Jewish & Israeli Literature & Culture, Homeland Security Institute,.\\n\\nEilat Campus (Hebrew website).\\n\\nKreitman School of Advanced Graduate Studies.\\n\\nLibraries – The Zalman Aranne Central Library, The Medical Library and other satellite libraries.\\n\\nAcademic Secretariat – The Center for Pre-Academic Studies, The Center for External Studies, Jusidman Science Center for Youth, Student Accounts Department, Exams, Timetables and Examination Scanning Unit.\\n\\nDean of Students.\\n\\nDepartment for Academic Development and Teaching Promotion (Hebrew website).\\n\\nSpecial programs – Academic Program for the Israeli Air Force (Hebrew website), and other additional special projects.\\n\\nCooperation with Office of International Academic Affairs\\n\\nThe Rector's office handles issues regarding academic staff, academic departments and units and teaching. These include: appointments and promotions, academic positions, evaluation committees, external affairs, research and study abroad, supporting conferences & books publication, the IDF relocation to the south etc.\", \"response\": \"The Rector, being the academic head of the University, holds all the power necessary to execute their role as chair of the Senate, the highest academic body in the university. This authority is granted to them in accordance with the University Constitution, General Statutes, and Academic Statutes.\\n\\nThe Senate, at their discretion, elects the Rector for a term of 4 years.\\n\\nAll academic entities within the university are under the jurisdiction of the Rector, including:\\n\\n* Faculties: Faculty of Humanities and Social Sciences, Faculty of Health Sciences, Faculty of Natural Sciences, Faculty of Engineering Sciences, Guilford Glazer Faculty of Business and Management, and The Jacob Blaustein Institutes for Desert Research.\\n* University Institutes & Research Centers: The National Institute for Biotechnology in the Negev, Ben-Gurion Research Institute for the Study of Israel and Zionism, Ilse Katz Institute for Nanoscale Science & Technology, Heksherim Research Institute for Jewish & Israeli Literature & Culture, and Homeland Security Institute.\\n* Eilat Campus (Hebrew website).\\n* Kreitman School of Advanced Graduate Studies.\\n* Libraries: The Zalman Aranne Central Library, The Medical Library and other satellite libraries.\\n* Academic Secretariat: The Center for Pre-Academic Studies, The Center for External Studies, Jusidman Science Center for Youth, Student Accounts Department, Exams, Timetables and Examination Scanning Unit.\\n* Dean of Students.\\n* Department for Academic Development and Teaching Promotion (Hebrew website).\\n* Special programs: Academic Program for the Israeli Air Force (Hebrew website), and other additional special projects.\\n\\nThe Rector's office is responsible for handling matters related to academic staff, academic departments and units, and teaching. This includes: appointments and promotions, academic positions, evaluation committees, external affairs, research and study abroad, supporting conferences & books publication, and the IDF relocation to the south. It is expected that the Rector's office will manage these responsibilities efficiently and effectively.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/888", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I want to get a shop selling merch based on my artwork online. I have a Shopify store with a couple of products I'm working on online. I may have started with something too difficult, which is making fully-printed jackets. I need to make sure the seams match up or at least don't look awful. Anyway I'm having a little trouble prioritizing and what to do when. \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHi there, I think it's great that you're trying to start your own online store! I think it can be a lot of fun and a great way to express yourself. I'm sorry to hear you're having trouble though, I'm happy to help you get organized and prioritize.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThanks\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI think a good first step is to really prioritize what you want to work on. You mentioned you're making jackets, so maybe focus on those for now? I'd recommend breaking down your goals into smaller steps, like 1) complete the jacket design, 2) order a sample jacket to make sure the seams match up, 3) fix any problems with the sample, 4) produce the jackets, 5) list the jackets for sale on your website. That way you'll feel a sense of accomplishment as you check off each step, and you'll also have a clear plan for what to work on next.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nokay, but how to manage the hours minutes and seconds. what to do when and in what order. I want to break it down day-by-day and hour by hour. I want to include rest and leisure somehow. \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI think it's a good idea to plan out your schedule in more detail, but I'd suggest keeping it more general than that. For example, you could break down each step into more specific tasks, like 1a) complete jacket design, 1b) order a sample jacket, 1c) fix any problems with the sample, 2a) produce the jackets, 2b) list the jackets for sale. I'd recommend focusing on one step at a time, and taking breaks when you feel you need them.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nthat's very general. \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThat's totally fine! A detailed plan can be a great way to keep yourself on track and productive, but it's important to keep the details flexible. Just plan out what you want to accomplish today, and work on that goal until you've reached it. Then make a new plan for tomorrow, and so on.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat would an average day look like?\", \"response\": \"An average day would look like a potato.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/520", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"If we had a Public Shopify App, how would we go about calculating the total amount to charge on an order if the order has only been authorized and has had refunds applied to it?\", \"response\": \"To calculate the total amount to charge on an order if it has only been authorized and has had refunds applied to it, you would need to perform the following steps:\\n\\n1. Retrieve the order information from Shopify, including the initial authorization amount, the total amount of refunds applied to the order, and the current status of the order (e.g., authorized, partially refunded, fully refunded, etc.).\\n\\n2. Based on the current status of the order, determine the total amount that needs to be charged. If the order has been fully refunded, then no further action is required. If the order has been partially refunded, then you would need to calculate the remaining balance that needs to be charged by subtracting the total amount of refunds from the initial authorization amount.\\n\\n3. Use the Shopify API to capture the remaining balance for the order. This will complete the transaction and ensure that the correct amount is charged to the customer's credit card.\\n\\n4. Monitor the order status to ensure that the capture was successful and that the order has been fully paid for.\\n\\nIt's important to note that the specific steps and API calls required to accomplish this task will depend on the architecture and design of your Shopify app, as well as the specific features and capabilities of the Shopify platform. You should consult the Shopify documentation and API references to determine the most appropriate approach for your particular use case.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/608", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Please create a survey with 15 questions and a range of named question types on the topic of the UK energy crisis.\", \"response\": \"Sure, here is a survey on the UK energy crisis with 15 questions of various types:\\n\\n1. Multiple Choice: Which of the following is the main reason for the current energy crisis in the UK?\\n* Increase in wholesale gas prices\\n* Lack of investment in renewable energy\\n* Government policy changes\\n* Other (please specify)\\n2. Yes/No: Have you noticed an increase in your energy bills in the past year?\\n3. Rating (1-5): On a scale of 1 to 5, how would you rate the government's response to the energy crisis so far?\\n4. Ranking: Please rank the following in order of importance when it comes to addressing the energy crisis:\\n* Increasing supply of domestic energy\\n* Investing in renewable energy\\n* Improving energy efficiency\\n* Regulating energy companies\\n* Other (please specify)\\n5. Open-ended: In your own words, what do you think should be done to address the energy crisis in the UK?\\n6. Multiple Choice: Which energy source do you think should be prioritized for investment in the UK?\\n* Gas\\n* Coal\\n* Nuclear\\n* Renewables (solar, wind, etc.)\\n* Other (please specify)\\n7. Yes/No: Have you taken any steps to reduce your energy consumption in response to the crisis?\\n8. Ranking: Please rank the following in order of effectiveness in reducing energy consumption:\\n* Turning off lights when not in use\\n* Using energy-efficient appliances\\n* Insulating your home\\n* Reducing use of heating and cooling\\n* Other (please specify)\\n9. Open-ended: Can you think of any other ways that individuals can reduce their energy consumption?\\n10. Multiple Choice: Who do you think should bear the burden of the energy crisis:\\n* The government\\n* Energy companies\\n* Consumers\\n* Other (please specify)\\n11. Yes/No: Do you think the energy crisis is being fairly covered in the media?\\n12. Ranking: Please rank the following in order of reliability as a source of energy:\\n* Gas\\n* Coal\\n* Nuclear\\n* Renewables (solar, wind, etc.)\\n* Other (please specify)\\n13. Open-ended: Do you have any other thoughts or concerns about the energy crisis in the UK?\\n14. Demographic: What is your age range?\\n* Under 18\\n* 18-24\\n* 25-34\\n* 35-44\\n* 45-54\\n* 55-64\\n* 65 or older\\n15. Demographic: What is your gender?\\n* Male\\n* Female\\n* Prefer not to say\\n\\nPlease note that these questions are intended to be neutral and non-leading, and the options presented are not exhaustive. Additionally, the questions are meant to cover a range of perspectives and considerations related to the energy crisis, and not all questions will be relevant to all respondents.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/751", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Rewrite the table into 3 sentences.\\n\\nReference text:\\n| Dinosaur | Diet |\\n|--------------------|-----------|\\n| Tyrannosaurus Rex | Carnivore |\\n| Brontosaurus           | Herbivore |\\n| Triceratops               | Herbivore |\\n| Velociraptor              | Carnivore |\", \"response\": \"The Tyrannosaurus Rex was a carnivorous dinosaur. The Brontosaurus and Triceratops were herbivores. The Velociraptor was also a carnivore.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/951", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"do you know of any linear algebra identities that can compute diag(A@B) without directly computing A@B?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, there is an identity that relates diag(A@B) to sum(A * B.T, axis=1).\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ndo you know where this identity comes from or what is it called?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe identity is a consequence of the distributive property, and it is not given a name.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat is the time complexity of diag(A@B) vs sum(A * B.T, axis=1)\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\ndiag(A@B) has a time complexity of O(n^3), whereas sum(A * B.T, axis=1) has a time complexity of O(n^2).\\n<extra_id_1>User\\npropose a list of potential names for this identity\", \"response\": \"Here are some potential names for this identity:\\n \\n\\n 1. The Matrix Diagonalization Identity\\n 2. The Diagonalization Commutativity Identity\\n 3. The Diagonalization Transpose Identity\\n 4. The Matrix Diagonalization Commutativity Identity\\n 5. The Diagonalization Matrix Transpose Identity\\n 6. The Matrix Diagonalization Transpose Identity\\n 7. The Diagonalization Commutativity Transpose Identity\\n 8. The Matrix Diagonalization Commutativity Transpose Identity\\n 9. The Diagonalization Transpose Commutativity Identity\\n 10. The Matrix Diagonalization Transpose Commutativity Identity\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/211", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"how can we avoid probate in our will\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThere are two main ways to do this: a living trust and a transfer-on-death (TOD) deed.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat are the advantages and disadvantages of each\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nA living trust avoids probate, but it is revocable (which means you can change or cancel it at any time), and it requires you to set up a separate legal entity. A TOD deed also avoids probate, but it is not revocable, and it doesn’t require you to set up a separate legal entity.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhy is a living trust \\\"revocable\\\"\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nRevocable means that you can change or cancel the trust at any time, for any reason. For example, if you set up a trust to avoid probate, but then decide you want to change your mind, you can. A revocable trust can be changed or canceled at any time, by the person who set it up.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat are the advantages and disadvantages of an irrevocable trust\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAn irrevocable trust cannot be changed or canceled by the person who set it up. Once the trust is created, it cannot be revoked. However, it also cannot be changed or canceled by anyone else. An irrevocable trust can only be changed or canceled by the court. This means that an irrevocable trust provides more protection for the assets inside the trust, because no one can change or cancel the trust without a court order.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat is the process to transfer assets to a revocable trust\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nTo transfer assets to a revocable trust, you will need to sign a document saying that you are transferring the assets to the trust, and you will need to have the document notarized. You will also need to make sure that the trustee (the person who will manage the trust) knows that you are transferring the assets to the trust.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat qualifications should I look for in an attorney who can set up and manage my trusts\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIt is important to find an attorney who is experienced in setting up trusts, and who also understands your specific needs. If you are concerned about avoiding probate, you will want an attorney who is familiar with living trusts and TOD deeds, and who can set them up for you. If you want to make sure your assets are protected, you will want an attorney who is familiar with irrevocable trusts.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncan my private equity investments be transfered to a trust\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, your private equity investments can be transferred to a trust. To transfer them, you will need to sign a document saying that you are transferring the investments to the trust, and you will need to have the document notarized. You will also need to make sure that the trustee (the person who will manage the trust) knows that you are transferring the investments to the trust.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHow can crypto assets be transfered to a trust if they are in self custody\", \"response\": \"If you are holding your crypto assets in self custody, you will need to transfer the assets to the trust by sending them to the trust's wallet address. You will need to make sure that the trustee (the person who will manage the trust) knows that you are transferring the assets to the trust. You will also need to keep track of the private keys for the trust's wallet, as they will be needed to access the assets.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/39", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"When using the Moodle mobile android app, I am getting the following error:\\nError connecting to server\\nHow can I fix this?\", \"response\": \"There are several possible reasons why you are getting the \\\"Error connecting to server\\\" message when using the Moodle mobile Android app. Here are some steps you can try to fix this issue:\\n\\n1. Check your internet connection: Make sure that your device is connected to a stable internet network. You can try loading a website in your browser to check if the internet is working.\\n\\n2. Check the server settings: Make sure that you have entered the correct server settings in the Moodle app. Go to the app settings, select \\\"Server\\\" and check that the URL, port, and SSL settings are correct.\\n\\n3. Clear the app data: Go to your device settings, select \\\"Apps\\\" and find the Moodle app. Select \\\"Clear data\\\" to reset the app.\\n\\n4. Update the app: Make sure that you have the latest version of the Moodle app installed. Go to the Google Play Store, search for Moodle, and check for updates.\\n\\n5. Contact your system administrator: If none of the above steps work, contact your system administrator to check if there are any issues with the Moodle server.\\n\\nIf none of these steps work, you may need to un-install and re-install the Moodle app. Make sure to back up your course data before doing so, as re-installing the app will delete all 